From 0fb8823d816330791fd58be344b18aaaba195fa8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 09:01:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] feat(libkernel): build for a lifted guest

Read the timestamp counter through GuestCpu, call guest thread entries
and exception handlers through it, and leave out the x86 assembly for
sigsetjmp, siglongjmp, getcontext and their kin in lifted builds, where
the runtime provides the jumps and context switching reports itself as
not implemented. A handler raised on a lifted thread sees the guest
registers of the thread's last call. ParamJsonParser's object members
become a complete type so that clang accepts the recursive value.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015taLuK6Ak1pT1P849L2eqq
